# TLS in front of Etheroute with Caddy - the simplest option on Windows, and
# the one that gets and renews its own certificate.
#
#   winget install CaddyServer.Caddy
#   caddy run --config deploy\Caddyfile          (from the project folder)
#   caddy start --config deploy\Caddyfile        (in the background)
#
# Needs: a domain whose A record points at this machine's public IP, and
# ports 80 and 443 forwarded to it. If you cannot open ports (a shared or
# school network), use the Cloudflare Tunnel route in DEPLOYMENT.md instead.
#
# Then in .env:  PORT=3000  NODE_ENV=production  TRUST_PROXY=true
# and restart the app: it listens on 3000 for Caddy alone, sees the real
# client address through X-Forwarded-For, and turns on its production
# headers and rate limits.

your-domain.com {
    encode zstd gzip
    request_body {
        max_size 200KB
    }
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3000 {
        header_up X-Real-IP {remote_host}
    }
}
